WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:15.345
At last Buldeo finished telling his stories.

2
00:00:16.966 --> 00:00:18.727
The villagers left the fig tree.

3
00:00:20.048 --> 00:00:23.570
They rushed toward Messua's hut, waving clubs and knives.

4
00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.032
They all carried torches.

5
00:00:26.052 --> 00:00:29.855
"Let's burn down the sorcerers' hut!"

6
00:00:30.535 --> 00:00:31.756
people yelled angrily.

7
00:00:33.952 --> 00:00:36.614
The crowd reached the hut and tore off the door.

8
00:00:37.935 --> 00:00:41.578
Everyone expected to see Messua and her husband trapped inside.

9
00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:49.583
Instead, stretched out on the bed with his paws crossed, was a fierce black panther.

10
00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:54.567
Bagheera slowly raised his head, flashing sharp white teeth.

11
00:00:56.028 --> 00:00:57.409
The villagers screamed.

12
00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.172
Then, in a panic, they scrambled to get outside.

13
00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.751
They raced to their huts and slammed shut the doors.

14
00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.855
Mowgli stepped out of the shadows and grinned.

15
00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:13.818
"That was a good plan, Bagheera!"

16
00:01:13.838 --> 00:01:18.502
"Thank you," the panther said proudly as he licked his paws.

17
00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:21.725
"The villagers won't come out until daylight.

18
00:01:22.205 --> 00:01:23.286
Let's get some rest now."

19
00:01:26.108 --> 00:01:30.012
When Mowgli woke the next day, he saw Rann, the hawk.

20
00:01:31.788 --> 00:01:34.791
"I have a message from Mother Wolf," the bird called.

21
00:01:34.811 --> 00:01:38.314
"Messua and her husband are safe in the new village.

22
00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:39.755
It is near a marsh."

23
00:01:42.678 --> 00:01:44.139
Mowgli waved happily.

24
00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:45.420
"Thank you!"

25
00:01:46.881 --> 00:01:48.803
Then he went off to tell Bagheera.

26
00:01:52.927 --> 00:01:56.089
"The people are still huddled indoors," Bagheera said.

27
00:01:56.109 --> 00:01:59.032
"Why don't we go hunting and forget about them?"

28
00:02:00.324 --> 00:02:01.604
Mowgli shook his head.

29
00:02:01.624 --> 00:02:03.625
"I'm sorry, Bagheera.

30
00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:06.006
I have to finish what I started.

31
00:02:06.646 --> 00:02:08.166
It's the law of the jungle.

32
00:02:09.107 --> 00:02:13.028
Those who break rules must be punished, remember?"

33
00:02:13.948 --> 00:02:14.968
Bagheera shrugged.

34
00:02:14.988 --> 00:02:17.469
"Where can I find Hathi?"

35
00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:18.769
Mowgli asked.

36
00:02:18.789 --> 00:02:21.250
"Hathi?" Bagheera said.

37
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.050
"I don't know.

38
00:02:23.531 --> 00:02:24.891
He feeds wherever he wants."

39
00:02:26.351 --> 00:02:28.372
"Can you find him and bring him to me?"

40
00:02:29.004 --> 00:02:31.305
Bagheera gave Mowgli a puzzled look.

41
00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.746
"I can't give orders to the master of the jungle."

42
00:02:35.627 --> 00:02:36.847
"Please, Bagheera."

43
00:02:37.828 --> 00:02:39.628
Then Mowgli had an idea.

44
00:02:39.648 --> 00:02:46.431
"If Hathi won't come, say these words: the sacking of the fields.

45
00:02:47.492 --> 00:02:50.073
Trust me, that will make him follow you."

46
00:02:50.093 --> 00:02:53.334
"'The sacking of the fields'?"

47
00:02:53.954 --> 00:02:56.835
Bagheera repeated the words until he remembered them.

48
00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.460
Then off he ran.

49
00:03:03.381 --> 00:03:05.882
It was dark when Bagheera finally returned.

50
00:03:06.923 --> 00:03:09.703
To Mowgli's relief, Hathi was with him.

51
00:03:10.464 --> 00:03:13.064
The elephant's three sons trailed after them.

52
00:03:13.084 --> 00:03:17.166
"Hello, Mowgli!"

53
00:03:17.646 --> 00:03:18.506
Hathi called.

54
00:03:19.846 --> 00:03:21.767
Mowgli greeted the old elephant.

55
00:03:22.987 --> 00:03:24.808
Then he turned to Bagheera.

56
00:03:25.448 --> 00:03:30.510
"I'm going to tell you a story about a wise elephant," Mowgli said.

57
00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:34.971
Bagheera looked startled, but he gave Mowgli a nod.

58
00:03:34.991 --> 00:03:39.752
"This elephant once got caught in a hunter's trap."

59
00:03:40.893 --> 00:03:42.413
Mowgli glanced at Hathi.

60
00:03:43.433 --> 00:03:47.975
In the moonlight everyone could see a long white scar on his side.

61
00:03:49.035 --> 00:03:52.456
It looked as if someone had hit him with a red-hot whip.

62
00:03:54.384 --> 00:03:58.127
"Men came to take him from the trap," Mowgli continued.

63
00:03:58.147 --> 00:04:02.912
"But he was very strong and broke free of the ropes.

64
00:04:04.573 --> 00:04:07.335
He went away until his wound healed.

65
00:04:09.377 --> 00:04:13.581
Then one night he came back with some other elephants."

66
00:04:15.763 --> 00:04:16.744
He looked at Hathi.

67
00:04:16.764 --> 00:04:18.845
"What happened next?"

68
00:04:19.966 --> 00:04:21.448
Hathi finished the story.

69
00:04:21.904 --> 00:04:24.246
"We stomped on the men's fields.

70
00:04:26.028 --> 00:04:27.409
We ate their crops.

71
00:04:27.829 --> 00:04:29.911
We tore the roofs off their huts.

72
00:04:31.813 --> 00:04:33.935
And then He paused.

73
00:04:33.955 --> 00:04:37.258
"We let the wild jungle in.

74
00:04:38.959 --> 00:04:41.722
It grew back and swallowed up everything."

75
00:04:43.463 --> 00:04:45.445
Mowgli nodded, satisfied.

76
00:04:46.506 --> 00:04:48.828
The elephant swung his trunk to look at him.

77
00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:53.238
"How did you know about the sacking of the fields?"

78
00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:58.320
"Buldeo told that story one night," Mowgli said.

79
00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.441
"I guess he tells the truth once in a while."

80
00:05:01.461 --> 00:05:04.682
"What do you want from me?"

81
00:05:05.003 --> 00:05:05.803
Hathi asked.

82
00:05:05.823 --> 00:05:10.985
"The people living in this village are cruel," Mowgli explained.

83
00:05:11.005 --> 00:05:14.427
"They hurt Messua and her husband.

84
00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.908
They were planning to kill me.

85
00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:21.086
And then they were going to kill Messua with the red flower.

86
00:05:22.487 --> 00:05:24.408
It's only right to punish them."

87
00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:27.990
Bagheera shivered and dropped down low.

88
00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:31.753
Now he understood why Mowgli had sent for
